    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d845">

                <pb facs="0926" n="640" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg640"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 341.622a/122a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        German Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bernstorff</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1919</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 4, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Refferring to previous
                    correspondence concerning the action of the British authorities in removing from
                    the American S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">China</hi> certain German and
                    Austro-Hungarian subjects, I have the honor to inquire whether you can inform me
                    whether any of the persons removed from that vessel were incorporated in the
                    armed forces of Germany, Austria, or Turkey.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
